    {
      "id": "2071762782014624213",
      "text": "China’s Zhipu AI is reportedly catching up to Anthropic in AI-powered vulnerability detection.\n\nGLM-5.2 is an open-weight model that can be downloaded, modified, and run publicly. \n\nIn Semgrep’s IDOR detection test, it reportedly reached:\n\n> 39% F1 score on IDOR detection\n> Higher than Claude Code’s 32–37% range\n> Around $0.17 per vulnerability found\n> Open access, unlike restricted Claude Mythos\n\nThe concern is not that GLM-5.2 beats U.S. models everywhere. It still trails on broader benchmarks.\n\nThe issue is narrower and more serious: open models are starting to match frontier systems in cybersecurity tasks.",
      "author": {
